{
  "raw": {
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042253": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer - Education - EU Conexus (Specified Purpose up to 31/10/2028)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Assistant Lecturer - Education - EU Conexus (Specified Purpose up to 31/10/2028) Vacancy I.D .: 042253 - Assistant Lecturer - Education - EU Conexus (Specified Purpose up to 31/10/2028) Contract : Whole-time, Specified Purpose Contract up to 31/10/2028 Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Assistant Lecturer is €47,572- €64,372 p.a. (rates effective 01/06/2026). SETU invites applications to the post of Assistant Lecturer in Education (EU Conexus) within the Faculty of Education and Lifelong Learning. The role will be instrumental in the delivery of the objectives of the EU-CONEXUS European University Alliance across SETU. The role will involve curriculum design and development with a specific focus on micro-credentials and innovation in programme delivery. Responsibilities will include programme development, curriculum design and teaching to include delivery of short, flexible awards including micro-credentials, both in an online and blended format. The role will include teaching and learning, and research related to EU-CONEXUS themes, and will require active engagement with the EU-CONEXUS university partners across Europe. The role will primarily focus on the activity of the EU-CONEXUS Alliance, particularly the delivery of education and innovation outputs. This role will be part of SETU’s EU-CONEXUS team and will involve active collaboration with colleagues in the EU-CONEXUS university partners across Europe. As a SETU-wide post, travel between campuses will be required from time to time to engage in role-related duties. Availability for occasional after-hours work and/or international travel is required as needed. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 06-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042253 Closing Date : 27-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042252": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer Education for Sustainable Development (Specified Purpose up to 31/10/2028)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Assistant Lecturer Education for Sustainable Development (Specified Purpose up to 31/10/2028) Vacancy I.D .: 042252 - Assistant Lecturer Education for Sustainable Development (Specified Purpose up to 31/10/2028) Contract : Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract up to 31/10/2028 Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Assistant Lecturer is €47,572- €64,372 p.a. (rates effective 01/06/2026). SETU invites applications for an Assistant Lecturer in Education for Sustainable Development within the Department of Education in the Faculty of Education and Lifelong Learning. The role will involve curriculum design and development, with a specific focus on ESD (Education for Sustainable Development). The role will form part of the EU-Conexus alliance in SETU, the European University alliance in SETU. Responsibilities will include programme development, curriculum design and teaching to include delivery of short, flexible awards including micro-credentials. The role will include teaching, research (on specific EU Conexus projects) and engagement (with EU Conexus partners across Europe). The role will primarily focus on the next phase of the European University alliance EU-Conexus called LevelUp and the delivery of outputs relating to the SETU work packages in this initiative. This role will be part of the EU Conexus team in SETU and work with colleagues across a number of disciplines. It also involves working with 8 EU Universities who are members of the EU-CONEXUS European University Alliance. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 06-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042252 Closing Date : 27-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042248": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer/Lecturer in Pharmaceutical Science (Organic Chemistry)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Assistant Lecturer/Lecturer in Pharmaceutical Science (Organic Chemistry) Vacancy I.D.: 042248 - Assistant Lecturer/Lecturer in Pharmaceutical Science (Organic Chemistry) Contract : Post One: 2-Year Whole-Time Fixed Term contract. Post Two: 6 months Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract. Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Assistant Lecturer is €47,572 - €64,372 p.a. (rates effective 01/06/2026).The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Lecturer is €69,625 - €107,727 p.a. (rates effective 01/06/2026). The Department of Science at South East Technological University invites applicants for the position of Assistant Lecturer/Lecturer in Pharmaceutical Science in the area of Organic Chemistry. The overall objective of this lecturer position is to facilitate the delivery of education to undergraduate and postgraduate students in the Department of Science at South East Technological University, Waterford Campus. Interviews for this position are expected to be held in Nov 2026, with the appointee to commence in the post in Jan 2027, subject to submission of all pre-employment documentation. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 08-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042248 Closing Date : 29-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042246": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer/Lecturer in Pharmaceutical Science (Physical/Inorganic Chemistry)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Assistant Lecturer/Lecturer in Pharmaceutical Science (Physical/Inorganic Chemistry) Vacancy I.D. : 042246 - Assistant Lecturer/Lecturer in Pharmaceutical Science (Physical/Inorganic Chemistry) Contract : 1 x permanent whole-time contract and 1 x 6-month wholte-time specified purpose contract Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Assistant Lecturer is €47,572 - €64,372 p.a. (rates effective 01/06/2026). The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Lecturer is €69,625 - €107,727 p.a. (rates effective 01/06/2026). The Department of Science at South East Technological University invites applicants for the position of Assistant Lecturer/Lecturer in Pharmaceutical Science in the area of Physical and/or Inorganic Chemistry. The overall objective of this lecturer position is to facilitate the delivery of education to undergraduate and postgraduate students in the Department of Science at South East Technological University, Waterford Campus. Interviews for this position are expected to be held in Nov 2026, with the appointee to commence in the post in Jan 2027, subject to submission of all pre-employment documentation. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 08-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042246 Closing Date : 29-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042166": {
      "title": "Vacancy: 042166 - Assistant Staff Officer - Functional Support Contract: Fixed Term - 2 years Salary: Assistant Staff Officer salary scale: €39,490 - €56,015 (Based on rates effective 1 June 2026) During this exciting time of strategic development, growth and change for SETU, we are seeking candidates with strong interpersonal, organisational, and ICT skills . The post holder s must have the ability to work in a tightly controlled and deadline driven environment. The successful candidate s will carry out tasks appropriate to a Grade IV role as assigned by the relevant manager and will work closely with colleagues across all SETU campuses . As vacancies arise in administrative roles across SETU, the functional support officers will provide administration support until a recruitment process can be completed. The expected duration in any given area will be a maximum of 12 weeks. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Assistant Staff Officer - Functional Support (Fixed Term, 2 years) Vacancy ID : 042166 Closing Date : 30-Oct-2026 12:00 Vacancy: 042166 - Assistant Staff Officer - Functional Support Contract: Fixed Term - 2 years Salary: Assistant Staff Officer salary scale: €39,490 - €56,015 (Based on rates effective 1 June 2026) During this exciting time of strategic development, growth and change for SETU, we are seeking candidates with strong interpersonal, organisational, and ICT skills . The post holder s must have the ability to work in a tightly controlled and deadline driven environment. The successful candidate s will carry out tasks appropriate to a Grade IV role as assigned by the relevant manager and will work closely with colleagues across all SETU campuses . As vacancies arise in administrative roles across SETU, the functional support officers will provide administration support until a recruitment process can be completed. The expected duration in any given area will be a maximum of 12 weeks. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042144": {
      "title": "Development Coordinator Philanthropy & Partnerships – Grade V (Specified Purpose)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/10/2026 Development Coordinator Philanthropy & Partnerships – Grade V (Specified Purpose) Vacancy I.D: 042144 - Development Coordinator Philanthropy & Partnerships – Grade V (Specified Purpose Contract) Contract : 6 months wholetime specified purpose contract - with possibility of extension of a further six months Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Staff Officer is €52,763 - €63,107 p.a on a full-time basis (rates effective 01/06/2026). For contract durations of less than 12 months, the salary will be pro-rata. As the Development Coordinator, the appoinitee holds responsibility for the administration associated with a growing fundraising and philanthropy function. In this crucial support role, you will ensure that the Development & Alumni Manager and Alumni Officer have the operational stability required to build relationships and secure investment. This position will be responsible for managing the essential systems, data, and processes that underpin every successful donation and partnership. From processing gifts and reconciling finances to coordinating high-level donor meetings and conducting background research, your organisational skills will directly enable the team to meet its ambitious targets. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 29-Sep-2026 Vacancy ID : 042144 Closing Date : 20-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitmentpmss.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042256": {
      "title": "Head of Legal Affairs (Permanent)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Head of Legal Affairs (Permanent) Vacancy I.D.: 042256 - Head of Legal Affairs (Permanent) Contract : Permanent Whole-Time Contract Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the post is €90,005 - €115,759 per annum on a full-time basis (rates effective 01/06/2026). The Head of Legal Affairs will be a senior member of the Governance Unit reporting to the University Secretary. They will play a pivotal and supportive role working within a multidisciplinary function that encompasses legal affairs, internal audit, compliance, risk management, policy management, internal controls, and data protection. The postholder will contribute to the provision of strategic oversight and organisational intelligence along with specific legal advice that supports informed decision-making and provides institutional assurance. The role will promote the highest standards of professionalism and integrity as part of the University’s legal and governance framework which supports effective operations, robust compliance, and sound risk management. The Head of Legal Affairs will specifically provide expert legal advice throughout the organisation and contribute to the development of a strong governance culture that serves the interests of the University. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 08-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042256 Close Date : 29-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitmentpmss.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042184": {
      "title": "Irish Language Officer - Grade VI (Part Time - 2 year Specified Purpose)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 21/10/2026 Irish Language Officer - Grade VI (Part Time - 2 year Specified Purpose) Vacancy I.D: 042184 - Irish Language Officer - Grade VI (Part Time - 2 year Specified Purpose) / Oifigeach Gaeilge – Grád VI (Conradh leathama 2 bliana) Contract : Part Time, 2-Year Specified Purpose / Conradh leathama 2 bliana Salary : The gross salary applicable to the post of Grade VI is €58,476 - €71,440 p.a. on a full-time basis (as at 01/06/2026). As a half time post, a corresponding pro-rata salary will apply to the post. / Is é an t - olltuarastal is infheidhme maidir le post Ghrád VI ná is €58,476- €71,440.p.a. ar bhonn lánaimseartha (amhail 01/06/2026). Mar phost leath - ama, beidh tuarastal comhfhreagrach pro - rata i bhfeidhm maidir leis an bpost. SETU wishes to recruit an Irish Language Officer to monitor and record compliance with relevant legislative requirements as set out in the Official Languages Act 2003 and 2021, and to facilitate and progress actions set out in the University’s Irish Language Strategy. More broadly, the Irish Language Officer will be responsible for promoting, supporting and enhancing the use of the Irish language within SETU across all campuses of SETU, working with staff and students, to support the University to achieve its strategic objectives in this area. Is mian le SETU Oifigeach Gaeilge a earcú chun monatóireacht agus taifeadadh a dhéanamh ar chomhlíonadh na gceanglas reachtach ábhartha mar atá leagtha amach in Acht na dTeangacha Oifigiúla 2003 agus 2021, agus chun gníomhartha atá leagtha amach i Straitéis Ghaeilge na hOllscoile a éascú agus a chur chun cinn. Ar bhonn níos leithne, beidh an tOifigeach Gaeilge freagrach as úsáid na Gaeilge a chur chun cinn, a fheabhsú agus tacú léi laistigh de SETU ar fud gach campais de chuid SETU, ag obair le baill foirne agus le mic léinn, chun tacú leis an Ollscoil a cuid aidhmeanna agus cuspóirí straitéiseacha a bhaint amach sa réimse seo. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. Próiseas Iarratais: Iarratais trí chóras ríomh-earcaíochta SETU amháin. Ní ghlacfar le hiarratais i bhformáid ar bith eile. Logáil isteach, le do thoil, ar www.SETU.ie/vacancies chun tuilleadh sonraí a fháil agus chun iarratas a dhéanamh ar an bpost seo. Is é an dáta deiridh chun iarratais chomhlánaithe a fháil. Is faisnéis ghinearálta amháin an fhaisnéis a thugtar sa doiciméad seo agus níor cheart glacadh leis mar fhaisnéis chonarthach. #SETU Opening Date : 30-Sep-2026 Vacancy ID : 042184 Closing Date : 21-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitmentpmss.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=041590": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Social Care Work (Specified Purpose up to 31/08/2028)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Lecturer in Social Care Work (Specified Purpose up to 31/08/2028) Vacancy I.D.: 041590 - Lecturer in Social Care Work (Specified Purpose up to 21/08/2028) Contract : Whole-Time Specified Purpose up to 31/08/2028 Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Lecturer is €69,625 - €107,727 p.a. (rates effective 01/06/2026). The Department of Social Care & Early Childhood at South East Technological University invites applicants for the position of Lecturer in Social Care Work. The overall objective of this lecturer position is to facilitate the delivery of education to undergraduate and postgraduate students in the Department of Social Care & Early Childhood at South East Technological University, College Street, Waterford Campus. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 08-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 041590 Closing Date : 29-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=041905": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Veterinary Medicine (Pathology) (Permanent)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 26/10/2026 Lecturer in Veterinary Medicine (Pathology) (Permanent) Vacancy I.D.: 041905 - Lecturer in Veterinary Medicine (Pathology) (Permanent) Contract : Permanent Whole-Time Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Lecturer is €69,625 - €107,727 p.a. (rates effective 01/06/2026). The overall objective of this lecturer position is to contribute to the design, development and delivery of the Veterinary Medicine undergraduate programme in the Department of Veterinary Medicine at South East Technological University, Waterford Campus in conjunction with Teagasc Kildalton College and the Veterinary Distributed Clinical Network. This role will require working on both the SETU Waterford and Teagasc Kildalton College campuses. The lecturer will contribute their veterinary pathology knowledge and skills to the development, teaching and assessment strategies for our programme. SETU is seeking a highly motivated individual with personal drive and ambition, dedicated to making a significant and lasting contribution to animal welfare, our learners, and the veterinary sector and to the development of the University and the furtherance of its core values. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 22-Sep-2026 Vacancy ID : 041905 Closing Date : 26-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042257": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Researcher - BIOSHORE Project (Specified Purpose to September 2028)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Post Doctoral Researcher - BIOSHORE Project (Specified Purpose to September 2028) Vacancy I.D.: 042257 - Post Doctoral Researcher - BIOSHORE Project (Specified Purpose to September 2028) Contract : Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract up to 30/ 09/2028 Salary : The gross salary applicable to the post is €47,879 p.a. (Point 2 of Postdoctoral salary scale) – rate effective June 2026. SETU Waterford is seeking a highly motivated, experienced and innovative Postdoctoral Researcher to join our multidisciplinary research team. The successful candidate will contribute to an applied research project focused on the development, characterisation and evaluation of natural-based biostimulants and bioactive compounds for sustainable agricultural and crop-production. The BIOSHORE project aims to identify and develop natural-based compounds with potential to improve plant growth, crop productivity, nutrient-use efficiency, resilience to environmental stresses and overall crop quality, while supporting the transition towards more sustainable and environmentally friendly agricultural practices. The research will involve extraction, characterisation and evaluation of the natural products and bioactive compounds, followed by systematic laboratory controlled-environment, pot and field-based studies to assess their efficacy across a range of economically important crops and agricultural systems. The successful candidate will be expected to design and implement pot and field-trials to evaluate the effects of selected natural-based biostimulant formulations on different crops and production systems. These may include vegetable crops such as tomatoes and potatoes, fruit crops such as apples and vines as well as grassland and other relevant agricultural crops. The research will contribute to understanding the mode of action of the biostimulants and practical applications both under controlled and real-world growing conditions. The position requires strong expertise in experimental design, plant science/agronomy and the planning and implementation of replicated pot and field-trials, together with experience in extraction, preparation and characterisation of natural products or bioactive compounds. Experience with analytical techniques and instrumentation such as High Performance Liquid Chromatography and related analytical methods would be highly desirable. The candidate should have the ability to interpret analytical and biological datasets and establish relationships between compounds composition, application rates and plant responses. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 06-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042257 Close Date : 27-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : researchrecruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042324": {
      "title": "Vacancy: 042324 - Pro Rata Part Time Assistant Lecturer - Agricultural Science Contract: Specified Purpose - until 31 July 2027 Salary: Assistant Lecturer salary scale: €47,572 - €64,372 (Pro rata equivalent for 0.583333 FTE) (Based on rates effective 1 June 2026) SETU's Summerhill Road Campus in Wexford offers a diverse range of courses to both full-time and part-time students. Programmes at this campus cover various disciplines, including Social Care, Early Childhood Education, Art, Visual Communications and Design, Business, Farm Management, and Tourism and Event Management. The courses range from Level 6 to Level 10, providing opportunities for students at different stages of their academic journeys. The Summerhill Road Campus is known for its collaborative approach, fostering strong connections with local communities, businesses, and the social care sector. South East Technological University wishes to appoint a Pro Rata Part Time Assistant Lecturer – Agricultural Science, based in SETU’s Summerhill Road Campus, Wexford. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Pro Rata Part Time Assistant Lecturer - Agricultural Science (Specified Purpose) Vacancy ID : 042324 Closing Date : 29-Oct-2026 12:00 Vacancy: 042324 - Pro Rata Part Time Assistant Lecturer - Agricultural Science Contract: Specified Purpose - until 31 July 2027 Salary: Assistant Lecturer salary scale: €47,572 - €64,372 (Pro rata equivalent for 0.583333 FTE) (Based on rates effective 1 June 2026) SETU's Summerhill Road Campus in Wexford offers a diverse range of courses to both full-time and part-time students. Programmes at this campus cover various disciplines, including Social Care, Early Childhood Education, Art, Visual Communications and Design, Business, Farm Management, and Tourism and Event Management. The courses range from Level 6 to Level 10, providing opportunities for students at different stages of their academic journeys. The Summerhill Road Campus is known for its collaborative approach, fostering strong connections with local communities, businesses, and the social care sector. South East Technological University wishes to appoint a Pro Rata Part Time Assistant Lecturer – Agricultural Science, based in SETU’s Summerhill Road Campus, Wexford. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042165": {
      "title": "Recruitment Staff Officer – Grade V (Permanent)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Recruitment Staff Officer – Grade V (Permanent) Vacancy I.D .: 042165 - Recruitment Staff Officer – Grade V (Permanent) Contract : Permanent Whole-Time Contract Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Staff Officer is €52,763 - €63,107 p.a. on a full-time basis (rates effective 01/06/2026). The Human Resources Office is seeking applications from a highly organised, dynamic and proactive individual to join the Recruitment Team and support the delivery of an effective, consistent and customer-focused recruitment service across SETU. The Recruitment Staff Officer – Grade V will play a key role in coordinating and administering the University's recruitment and selection processes, providing professional support to hiring managers and recruitment stakeholders, maintaining accurate recruitment records and data, and ensuring that recruitment activities progress efficiently and in accordance with University policies, procedures and relevant legislation. The role will have particular responsibility for the coordination of recruitment and selection activities, recruitment reporting, international recruitment and onboarding processes, employment permits and hosting agreements, Garda vetting, and the coordination of recruitment-related activity at campus level. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 06-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042165 Closing Date : 27-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitmentpmss.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=041684": {
      "title": "Vacancy: 041684 - Senior Staff Officer, Finance Contract: Specified Purpose - until 31 December 2027 Salary: Senior Staff Officer salary scale: €58,476 - €71,440 (based on rates effective 1 June 2026) SETU is seeking an experienced Accountant to join the Finance team in supporting the continued development of the University. The role will support the delivery of the objectives of the Finance Department across the wide range of activities within the Department, primarily focusing on Funded Projects, such as the TU Research and Innovation Supporting Enterprise (TU RISE) Scheme. The role will support the delivery of the objectives of the Finance Department across the wide range of activities within the Department, primarily focusing on Funded Projects, such as the TU Research and Innovation Supporting Enterprise (TU RISE) Scheme, working closely with stakeholders across the University. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Senior Staff Officer, Finance (Specified Purpose until Dec 2027) Vacancy ID : 041684 Closing Date : 19-Oct-2026 12:00 Vacancy: 041684 - Senior Staff Officer, Finance Contract: Specified Purpose - until 31 December 2027 Salary: Senior Staff Officer salary scale: €58,476 - €71,440 (based on rates effective 1 June 2026) SETU is seeking an experienced Accountant to join the Finance team in supporting the continued development of the University. The role will support the delivery of the objectives of the Finance Department across the wide range of activities within the Department, primarily focusing on Funded Projects, such as the TU Research and Innovation Supporting Enterprise (TU RISE) Scheme. The role will support the delivery of the objectives of the Finance Department across the wide range of activities within the Department, primarily focusing on Funded Projects, such as the TU Research and Innovation Supporting Enterprise (TU RISE) Scheme, working closely with stakeholders across the University. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042251": {
      "title": "SETU European University Alliance Institutional Lead (Specified Purpose to 31/10/2028)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 SETU European University Alliance Institutional Lead (Specified Purpose to 31/10/2028) Vacancy I.D.: 042251 - SETU European University Alliance Institutional Lead (Specified Purpose to 31/10/2028) Contract : Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the post is €90,005 - €115,759 per annum on a full-time basis (rates effective 01/06/2026). This is an exciting time for SETU as it prepares to deepen its involvement in the EU-CONEXUS European University Alliance. To support this objective, SETU is recruiting a SETU European University Alliance Institutional Lead to drive the next phase of EU-CONEXUS Alliance activity across our campuses. This role will be instrumental in achieving the objectives of the EU-CONEXUS Alliance strategy alongside the University’s own goals set out in its Strategic Plan 2023-28. Reporting to the EU-CONEXUS Executive Lead at SETU, the role will involve representing SETU within this international Alliance, supporting the development of key relationships our stakeholders, and oversee the delivery of key initiatives and project opportunities for SETU. The role will require strong cross-campus collaboration and extensive engagement with external stakeholders across varying sectors at regional, national and international levels. The SETU European University Alliance Institutional Lead will also work closely with the President of SETU along with other members of the Executive Management Team, key stakeholders across the university, and externally in the community. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 06-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042251 Closing Date : 27-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitmentpmss.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042304": {
      "title": "Vacancy: 042304 - Staff Officer - Finance Analyst Contract: Fixed Term, 3 years Salary: Staff Officer salary scale: €52,763 - €63,107 (based on rates effective 1 June 2026) SETU is seeking 3 x Finance Analysts to join the Finance team in supporting the continued development of the University. The roles will support the delivery of high-quality management reporting, financial insight and planning across SETU, working closely with the Senior Accountant and stakeholders across faculties and departments. The roles will form part of the Financial Planning & Analysis team, while also supporting finance integration and wider Finance priorities as required. The roles will support management accounting across SETU through financial analysis, planning and insight to support decision-making, Finance projects, ongoing process improvement and wider Finance priorities as required. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Staff Officer - Finance Analyst (Fixed Term, 3 years) Vacancy ID : 042304 Closing Date : 30-Oct-2026 12:00 Vacancy: 042304 - Staff Officer - Finance Analyst Contract: Fixed Term, 3 years Salary: Staff Officer salary scale: €52,763 - €63,107 (based on rates effective 1 June 2026) SETU is seeking 3 x Finance Analysts to join the Finance team in supporting the continued development of the University. The roles will support the delivery of high-quality management reporting, financial insight and planning across SETU, working closely with the Senior Accountant and stakeholders across faculties and departments. The roles will form part of the Financial Planning & Analysis team, while also supporting finance integration and wider Finance priorities as required. The roles will support management accounting across SETU through financial analysis, planning and insight to support decision-making, Finance projects, ongoing process improvement and wider Finance priorities as required. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042224": {
      "title": "Academic Unit Review Leads x6 (Confined SETU Competition - Specified Purpose)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Academic Unit Review Leads x6 (Confined SETU Competition - Specified Purpose) This is a confined competition open to SETU staff members. Applicants who are not currently employed at SETU are ineligible to apply. Vacancy I.D.: 042224 - Academic Unit Review Leads x6 (Confined SETU Competition - Specified Purpose) Contract : Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract up to June 2028 Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the post is €97,917 - €125,890 per annum (rates effective 01.06.2026). South East Technological University (SETU) is Ireland’s newest TU, designated in May 2022. The university has designed an organisational change programme that will support elevated performance in the delivery of educational programmes, in research and innovation, in mobilising regional alliances, and in building institutional capacity, resilience and sustainability. The Office of the Vice President Academic Affairs, Teaching and Learning plays a critical leadership role in the delivery of the change programme, with assessment enhancement and capacity building an important part of this. AUR (Academic Unit Review) leads are Technological Enhancement Fund (TEF) posts, one for each faculty within the University , to support faculties in the development, production and review stages of the Academic Review Process (AUR). The roles are extensions of the successful work of the ROaD project and draw from the outputs of that academic integration project as a baseline. Supporting the Heads of Faculties and Heads of Departments, they will enhance the review capacity of the faculty and assist in building a new strategically embedded academic portfolio across all of the activities of the faculty. The roles will also provide a coordinating university framework for ensuring appropriate university policies and strategic objectives are adequately addressed in the review processes. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. Opening Date : 16-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042224 Close Date : 30-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042250": {
      "title": "EU Conexus Administrator - Grade IV (Confined Competition - Specified Purpose up to 31/10/2028)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 26/10/2026 EU Conexus Administrator - Grade IV (Confined Competition - Specified Purpose up to 31/10/2028) Confined Competition:This is a confined competition limited to the Education and Training Candidate Sector Pool i.e., eligible administration & library staff within SETU, Technological Universities, Institutes of Technology and Education & Training Boards at specific grades. Vacancy I.D.: 042250 - EU Conexus Administrator - Grade IV (Confined Competition - Specified Purpose up to 31/10/2028) Contract : Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract up to 31/10/2028 Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Assistant Staff Officer is €39,490 - €56,015 p.a on a full-time basis (rates effective 01/06/2026) The successful candidate will work as part of the EU-CONEXUS team, appropriate to a Grade 4 Assistant Staff Officer role, supporting staff and management to deliver quality services to staff, students, and stakeholders. The position involves regular contact with students and staff at all levels both at SETU and at our international Alliance university partners where discretion, courtesy and judgement are exercised. The successful candidate will be required to be flexible while undertaking duties while promoting and maintaining best practice, and may be asked to travel between SETU campuses from time to time. The successful candidate will be required to have strong experience in administration, excellent interpersonal and communication skills, a high level of computer literacy, a proven track record of organisational abilities and the ability to work on their own initiative. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. Opening Date : 16-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042250 Closing Date : 26-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitmentpmss.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042024": {
      "title": "Grade IV Assistant Staff Officer –Academic Unit Review x6 (Specified Purpose up to June 2028)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 06/11/2026 Grade IV Assistant Staff Officer –Academic Unit Review x6 (Specified Purpose up to June 2028) Vacancy I.D.: 042024 - Grade IV Assistant Staff Officer –Academic Unit Review x6 (Specified Purpose up to June 2028) Contract : Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract up to June 2028 Salary : The gross salary applicable to the post of Assistant Staff Officer is currently €39,490 - €56,015 p.a. (rates effective 01/06/2026) Grade IV Assistant Staff Officer –Academic Unit Review are Technological Enhancement Fund (TEF) posts, one for each faculty within the University, to support faculties in the development, production and review stages of the Academic Review Process (AUR). Reporting to the Academic Unit Review (AUR) Lead, the appointee will provide a key supporting role in the planning, organising, administration and submission of academic unit reviews. This could include, but not be limited to, aspects around or related to project management governance, meeting and administrative organization, communication, , training, quality assurance support and document editing and production. The appointee may also be required to provide support to senior staff across the areas of the VP for Academic Affairs, Teaching and Learning including deputising for more senior administrative staff as the occasion demands. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 16-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042024 Closing Date : 06-Nov-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitmentpmss.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042255": {
      "title": "Head of Faculty - Health Sciences (Waterford) Senior Lecturer III (Permanent)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/11/2026 Head of Faculty - Health Sciences (Waterford) Senior Lecturer III (Permanent) Vacancy I.D.: 042255 - Head of Faculty - Health Sciences (Waterford) Senior Lecturer III (Permanent) Contract : Permanent Whole-Time Contract Salary : The Gross Salary Scale applicable to the post of Head of Faculty SL3 is €105,346 - €135,494 p.a. (rates effective 01/02/2026). South East Technological University (SETU) was established in 2022 and is both a regional and internationally oriented organisation with a focus on further enhancing its role as an exceptional quality-of-life driver within the regional, national and international higher education landscape. Our vision is to be a leading multi-campus technological university by 2030, an ambitious vision that reflects the development of a mature institution with an important leadership role in the regional economic and social landscape. Health Sciences is integral to our ambitious vision for higher education in the South East. On the Waterford campus, the Faculty of Health Sciences comprises the Department of Nursing and Health Care and the Department of Sport and Exercise Science, and includes the Nutrition Research Centre Ireland. The Faculty provides undergraduate, postgraduate and research education and activity across nursing, health care, sport, exercise, health promotion and related disciplines. This permanent post will be based in Waterford and will provide strategic, academic and operational leadership for the Faculty’s Waterford-based activities, while contributing to the coordination and development of Health Sciences across SETU. SETU is seeking an exceptional individual to lead and manage further innovation and development, working closely with the Senior Management Team of SETU; the Head of Department of Nursing and Health Care; the Head of Department of Sport and Exercise Science; faculty members and researchers in Health Sciences and across the University; professional services colleagues; and stakeholders regionally, nationally and internationally. Reporting to the President in the first instance, the postholder will play a pivotal role in the strategic development of the University as a whole, as well as in the further development of teaching and learning, research and innovation, and regional and international engagement. The successful candidate will also be responsible for the day-to-day leadership and management of the relevant Faculty activities based on the Waterford campus. This role requires a highly experienced and motivated individual with a strong work ethic, commitment to the highest professional standards, proven record of accomplishment, excellent communication and analytical skills and a team player who relishes new challenges with the ability to navigate change. The commitment to work collegially and productively with colleagues across SETU will be essential. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. In the upload section of the online application form, applicants are required to submit a) A detailed personal statement (the personal statement must be no longer than 1000 words) outlining why they wish to be considered for the post and where they consider their skills and experience meet the requirements of the position and should demonstrate strengths in relation to the following areas: i. An outline of applicant’s academic and professional leadership, research and scholarship. ii. Highlight the applicant’s active role to date in professional and academic activities. This may include areas such as research, engagement with external agencies/communities, collaboration with universities, interprofessional and cross discipline collaborations, development of initiatives in teaching and learning etc. iii. Evidence of the professional support that the applicant has provided to colleagues and students. iv. Demonstrate the applicant’s innovation in teaching, research or sectoral innovation and improvement methods. b) Applicants are also required to submit a CV and covering letter detailing previous relevant experience relating to this role. Please note: It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure all required documents are uploaded. The system may acknowledge submission even if the required application documentation is incomplete. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 13-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042255 Close Date : 03-Nov-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042384": {
      "title": "Knowledge Transfer Case Officer - Grade VII (Confined Competition Specified Purpose)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 26/10/2026 Knowledge Transfer Case Officer - Grade VII (Confined Competition Specified Purpose) Confined Competition: This is a confined competition limited to the Education and Training Candidate Sector Pool i.e., eligible administration & library staff within SETU, Technological Universities, Institutes of Technology and Education & Training Boards at specific grades. Vacancy I.D.: 042384 - Knowledge Transfer Case Officer - Grade VII (Confined Competition Specified Purpose) Contract : Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract up to 31/12/2027 Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Administrative Officer – Grade VII is €61,217- €79,584 p.a. (based on rates effective 01/06/2026) SETU is committed to achieving the objectives of the Technological University sector by ensuring that research, teaching, and learning are informed by societal challenges, aligned with the employment and skills needs of the region, and underpinned by strong, well-established partnerships with industry, employers, and local communities. The Knowledge Transfer Case Officer positions, one specialising in Life Sciences and the other in Manufacturing/Engineering , will work closely with the Head of Innovation & Commercialisation to coordinate, develop, and grow SETU's intellectual property (IP) portfolio within their respective disciplines and across the wider research landscape of the University. The post holders will actively support knowledge transfer, research impact, and the commercialisation of research outputs, ensuring that success in these areas contributes to the enhancement of SETU's reputation as a leading innovation and research partner. The successful candidates will collaborate closely with the Head of Innovation & Commercialisation, academic staff, researchers, and professional services colleagues across SETU to establish and nurture long-term strategic R&D partnerships with industry and external stakeholders. They will develop, promote, and deliver a broad range of research, innovation, and commercialisation support services to regional enterprise, civic, and community partners, helping to maximise the societal and economic impact of SETU's research and innovation activities. Applicants are required to indicate in the online application form which post they are applying to: • Knowledge Transfer Case Officer – Life Sciences • Knowledge Transfer Case Officer – Manufacturing/Engineering • Both positions Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. Opening Date : 16-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042384 Closing Date : 26-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : researchrecruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042424": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher AI / Digital Twins for ICT Infrastructure (24 Months Specified Purpose)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/11/2026 Postdoctoral Researcher AI / Digital Twins for ICT Infrastructure (24 Months Specified Purpose) Vacancy I.D .: 042424 - Postdoctoral Researcher AI / Digital Twins for ICT Infrastructure (24 Months Specified Purpose) Contract : Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the post is €49,890 - €53,925 p.a. (Research Ireland Postdoctoral Researcher [Level 2A] Point 3 – Point 6) as at June 2026 rates. Walton Institute is looking to hire a Postdoctoral Researcher in Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Digital Twins (DTs) for next-generation Information and Communication Technology (ICT) Infrastructure to conduct advanced academic research at the cutting edge of machine learning and digital communications, networks, and smart systems. The postdoctoral researcher will work on high-impact national and EU projects linked to some of the research areas of Transport, Data, Energy, Security, 6G, IoT and Quantum. Walton Institute is a partner in the Research Ireland Centres CONNECT for Future Networks and Rinn Quantum with strong collaborations across large EU projects such as the €18 M TransEuroOGS project (part of the EuroQCI which is building a secure communication infrastructure spanning the whole EU). The role will focus on the development of AI and Digital Twin tools and software packages for a range of use cases and applications related to the research areas outlined above. This could include next-generation networking, intelligent automation, cyber-physical systems, intelligent edge computing, network security and privacy and cybersecurity, blockchain-based network security, AI-driven energy harvesting, predictive traffic engineering, AI and digital twins for ICT, anomaly detection. The researcher will work closely with the Principal Investigator to ensure validation, compliance, scalability, and real-world applicability of these tools. Eligible applicants will have a PhD degree in Computer Science, Science, Computer Engineering or a related field. The candidate is required to have strong expertise in research and application of AI and Digital Twins to several use cases in at least one of the above research areas. If you are interested in working in a unique research organisation within the higher education sector, Walton institute offers a culture that promotes autonomy and the pursuit of individual interests and ideas. We're excited about opportunities that will create new technologies, advance existing ones and we will actively support the commercialisation process of these technologies. This provides you with the opportunity to explore your own creativity and work on cutting edge technologies across a variety of challenging projects, engaging and collaborating with like-minded people. Walton Institute ultimately offers flexibility in a great working environment for those looking to embark on a challenge. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 13-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042424 Close Date : 03-Nov-2026 12:00 Contact Email : researchrecruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042425": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher Experimental Quantum Optics / Nanophotonics x3 (24 Months Specified Purpose)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/11/2026 Postdoctoral Researcher Experimental Quantum Optics / Nanophotonics x3 (24 Months Specified Purpose) Vacancy I.D. : 042425 - Postdoctoral Researcher Experimental Quantum Optics / Nanophotonics x3 (24 Months Specified Purpose) Contract : Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the post is €49,890 - €53,925 p.a. (Research Ireland Postdoctoral Researcher [Level 2A] Point 3 – Point 6) as at June 2026 rates. Walton Institute is looking to hire 3 Postdoctoral Researchers in Experimental Quantum Optics / Nanophotonics to work on national and EU projects linked to the research area of quantum communication. Walton Institute in SETU is a lead partner in the Research Ireland Centre Rinn Quantum, a partner in the Research Ireland Centre CONNECT for Future Networks and Communications and a lead partner in the €18 M TransEuroOGS project (part of the EuroQCI which is building a secure communication infrastructure spanning the whole EU). The role will focus on experimental quantum optics for quantum communication networks, or experimental quantum nanophotonics for development of novel quantum metamaterials. Eligible applicants will have a PhD degree in Physics/ Engineering with an interest in quantum technology. If you are interested in working in a unique research organisation within the higher education sector, Walton institute offers a culture that promotes autonomy and the pursuit of individual interests and ideas. We're excited about opportunities that will create new technologies, advance existing ones and we will actively support the commercialisation process of these technologies. This provides you with the opportunity to explore your own creativity and work on cutting edge technologies across a variety of challenging projects, engaging and collaborating with like-minded people. Walton Institute ultimately offers flexibility in a great working environment for those looking to embark on a challenge. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. #SETU Opening Date : 13-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042425 Close Date : 03-Nov-2026 12:00 Contact Email : researchrecruitment.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheseturecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=042249": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Administrator - Grade IV (Confined Competition 1 Year Specified Purpose)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 26/10/2026 Undergraduate Administrator - Grade IV (Confined Competition 1 Year Specified Purpose) Confined Competition: This is a confined competition limited to the Education and Training Candidate Sector Pool i.e., eligible administration & library staff within SETU, Technological Universities, Institutes of Technology and Education & Training Boards at specific grades. Vacancy I.D.: Undergraduate Administrator - Grade IV Assistant Staff Officer (Confined Competition 1 Year Specified Purpose) Contract : 1-Year Whole-Time, Specified Purpose Contract Salary : The gross salary scale applicable to the grade of Assistant Staff Officer is €39,490 - €56,015 p.a on a full-time basis (rates effective 01/06/2026). The Faculty of Education and Lifelong Learning is the central agency responsible for promoting the growth and development of part-time, flexible courses including course marketing and promotion; course development, delivery and quality assurance; liaison with external partners including funding agencies and industry partners; central student advice and liaison. The Faculty works in partnership with all the other Faculties and with external partners to offer part- time and flexible courses, across levels 6-9, to the general public and to industry. The Department of Education offers teachers and educators a broad suite of undergraduate and postgraduate programmes in Education, including Adult Literacy; Community Education and Development; Initial Teacher Education for the Further Education and Training (FET) sector; Teaching and Learning; Technology-enhanced Learning and Educational Leadership. The post-holder will provide administrative support to the Department in all aspects of the Department’s undergraduate programme planning and delivery as well as administrative support to the School of Education and Lifelong Learning generally. Application Process: Applications must be made through the online recruitment system on SETU’s Vacancies page on the website. Please log onto SETU Vacancies for further details and to apply for this position. Applications will not be accepted by email, any other third-party website or in any other format. Garda Vetting may be required for particular posts. SETU is an equal opportunities employer. Opening Date : 16-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 042249 Closing Date : 26-Oct-2026 12:00 Contact Email : recruitmentpmss.wd@setu.ie Contact Number : Contact Person : Recruitment Team"
    }
  },
